</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Yan Song
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Zhongguancun Institute of Artificial Intelligence
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname"><span id="id6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">tianyuanhe@zgci.ac.cn</span>
</span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Pruning provides a practical solution to reduce the resources required to run large language models (LLMs) to benefit from their effective
capabilities as well as control their cost for training and inference.
Research on LLM pruning often ranks the importance of LLM parameters using their magnitudes and calibration-data activations and removes (or masks) the less important ones, accordingly reducing LLMs’ size.
However, these approaches primarily focus on preserving the LLM’s ability to generate fluent sentences, while neglecting performance on specific domains and tasks.
In this paper, we propose a simple yet effective pruning approach for LLMs that preserves task-specific capabilities while shrinking their parameter space.
<span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
We first analyze how conventional pruning minimizes loss perturbation under general-domain calibration and extend this formulation by incorporating task-specific feature distributions into the importance computation of existing pruning algorithms.
Thus, our framework computes separate importance scores using both general and task-specific calibration data, partitions parameters into shared and exclusive groups based on activation-norm differences, and then fuses their scores to guide the pruning process.
This design enables our method to integrate seamlessly with various foundation pruning techniques and preserve the LLM’s specialized abilities under compression.
</span>
Experiments on widely used benchmarks demonstrate that our approach is effective and consistently outperforms the baselines with identical pruning ratios and different settings.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Large language models, pruning, task-aware

</div><span id="footnotex1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnotetext"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">footnotetext: </span>Corresponding Author.</span></span></span>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models (LLMs) present outstanding performance across a diverse set of artificial intelligence (AI) tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.
However, their substantial size and intensive computational requirements pose significant challenges for deployment in resource-constrained environments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.
Pruning these models, i.e., selectively removing redundant or low-impact parameters, has emerged as a key strategy to lower inference latency and memory usage while preserving model capabilities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.
It not only alleviates computational overhead but also facilitates the adaptation of LLMs to downstream applications with limited labeled data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Many studies on LLM pruning mainly focus on preserving the generation capability of LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">kwon2022fast，sun2023simple</span>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>.
Early approaches prune the weights or entire substructures in a model that contribute least to its overall performance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>,
where they often require architectural modifications or extensive fine-tuning on large datasets to recover any lost performance.
Subsequent studies, such as SparseGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> and Wanda <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, prune models by measuring the importance of different parts of the model with criteria based on the magnitude of the weights and the computed activation values of the running examples from a calibration dataset.
The calibration data in these studies typically come from general-domain plain text and are used to identify the parameters that allow the model to produce fluent sentences.
These approaches perform well on conventional LLMs such as GPT-3 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> and LLaMA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> that have not undergone instruction-following fine-tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>.
However, by noticing that recent LLMs possess capabilities such as knowledge storage, instruction following, and question answering, and the parameters associated with these functions may not be highlighted by the calibration data,
it is thus of high risk that crucial parameters are potentially wrongly removed and leading to performance degradation across tasks.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>
Particularly, for scenarios such as summarization or domain-specific question answering, model pruning aims not only to shrink the model size but also to retain essential task-specific characteristics.
However, existing pruning approaches that aim at preserving the main ability of text generation for LLMs are not able to guarantee a desirable performance on tasks that require instruction following, since the models may expect various outputs under different instruction contexts with identical input and generic calibration data fails to highlight the weights critical for such conditional behaviors.
Therefore, there is an urgent need for a pruning approach that precisely identifies and preserves task-relevant parameters while effectively compressing the model.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22489v1/figures/model.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/255;" width="476" height="255" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
The overall process of our framework for LLM pruning.
The bottom part presents the LLM.
The top presents the pruning process for a particular parameter matrix in the LLM, where the general and task-specific calibration data (marked by the blue and purple colors, respectively) are used to compute the pruning scores of each parameter.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we propose a general LLM pruning framework designed to bridge the gap between generic model compression and task-specific model adaptation.
Our approach uses two calibration sources (i.e., general and task-specific scores) to compute activation-weighted magnitude scores with a standard pruning backend.
We then partition channels by activation-norm differences into shared, general-only, and task-only groups, aggregate the corresponding groupwise scores into a mixed importance, and prune the lowest-scoring weights.
Extensive experiments on WikiText-2 and other widely used benchmarks show that our approach effectively removes model parameters while maintaining comparable accuracy and perplexity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">The Approach</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our approach is a simple yet effective task-aware LLM pruning framework that is operated upon any fundamental pruning algorithms.
Specifically, our approach leverages a dual‐source pruning paradigm with calibration datasets from both general‐domain inputs <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and task‐specific examples <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, which together inform parameter importance through direct model activations.
With such data utilization through the LLM, our approach precisely identifies weights whose contributions are not significant across diverse contexts, enabling targeted pruning without compromising the LLM’s core capabilities.
Therefore, it is a high‐fidelity pruning strategy that combines general robustness with task‐level precision, ensuring streamlined efficiency at scale.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM Pruning</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In general, pruning
controls less relevant parameters in an LLM by
minimizing their impact on downstream task performance, <span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where the distribution of the features for the task data is represented by <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assuming we have a calibration dataset <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> instances following the feature distribution <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{(x,y^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{(x,y^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the input and the human-annotated output, respectively,
a straightforward solution to measure a model’s performance on a downstream task is to compute the loss on the calibration data <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>
Specifically, for a parameter matrix <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss function <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the expectation over the <span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">feature distribution <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\mathbf{W})=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\mathbf{W})=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> denoting the loss for a single sample between the model’s prediction <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathbf{W}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathbf{W}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the ground-truth label <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The gradient of the parameter, namely, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla L(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla L(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, describes the linear response of the loss to small changes in the parameters.
A pruning operation is viewed as applying a perturbation <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> in parameter space.
We define <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{ij}={W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{new}}-{W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>new</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>old</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{ij}={W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{new}}-{W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> to describe such parameter change for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> in the fully connected layer (<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>new</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>old</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{W}_{ij}^{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the pruned and original weight at position <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> in the weight matrix, respectively, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the difference of them in the corresponding position of <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>).
<span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
When a weight is pruned, it is equivalent to setting its value to zero, which leads to
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{ij}=-W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{ij}=-W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, and all other elements satisfy <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{kl}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{kl}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k,l)\neq(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k,l)\neq(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>
By performing a multivariate Taylor expansion of the loss at <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> and ignoring higher-order terms, one should obtain:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\mathbf{W}+\Delta\mathbf{W})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\mathbf{W}+\Delta\mathbf{W})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\mathbf{W})+\langle\nabla L(\mathbf{W}),\,\Delta\mathbf{W}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\mathbf{W})+\langle\nabla L(\mathbf{W}),\,\Delta\mathbf{W}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}+O(\|\Delta\mathbf{W}\|^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}+O(\|\Delta\mathbf{W}\|^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, when the original model parameters have been sufficiently trained and are near convergence, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla L(\mathbf{W})\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla L(\mathbf{W})\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the first-order perturbation is equivalent to be neglected.
The loss difference caused by pruning, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(\mathbf{W})=L(\mathbf{W}+\Delta\mathbf{W})-L(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(\mathbf{W})=L(\mathbf{W}+\Delta\mathbf{W})-L(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, approximates to</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(\mathbf{W})\approx\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(\mathbf{W})\approx\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the diagonal elements <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{ij,ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{ij,ij}</annotation></semantics></math> in the Hessian matrix <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathbf{W})=\nabla^{2}L(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathbf{W})=\nabla^{2}L(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math> measure the second-order curvature <span id="S2.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with respect to</span> the parameter <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{ij}=-W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{ij}=-W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> transforms the second-order term into <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}\,H_{ij,ij}\,\mathbf{W}_{ij}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}\,H_{ij,ij}\,\mathbf{W}_{ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which quantifies the
effect on the loss from pruning weight <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of second-order sensitivity.
<span id="S2.SS1.p1.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Therefore, given a pruning rate <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the goal of pruning algorithms subjects to find a pruning matrix <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the rate <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and minimizing the <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is written as</span></p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{W}}=\arg\min_{\Delta\mathbf{W}}\tfrac{1}{2}\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\Delta\mathbf{W}\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{W}}=\arg\min_{\Delta\mathbf{W}}\tfrac{1}{2}\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\Delta\mathbf{W}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">subject to</span><span id="S2.SS1.p1.6.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\mathbf{W}\|_{0}=r\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\mathbf{W}\|_{0}=r\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m40" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> counts the number of nonzero entries in a matrix and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\mathbf{W}\|_{0}=r\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\mathbf{W}\|_{0}=r\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> means that exactly an <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of the weights are pruned.
To facilitate the optimization of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), we introduce binary pruning indicators <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{ij}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{ij}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i,j}\alpha_{ij}=r\,\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i,j}\alpha_{ij}=r\,\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for a particular weight <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{ij}=-\alpha_{ij}\,W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{ij}=-\alpha_{ij}\,W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tfrac{1}{2}\,\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H(\mathbf{W})\,\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,(\Delta W_{ij})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,(\Delta W_{ij})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,(\alpha_{ij}W_{ij})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,(\alpha_{ij}W_{ij})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E6Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}\,\alpha_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}\,\alpha_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where off-diagonal Hessian entries are ignored.
Thus, the objective Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is rewritten as finding a set of optimal <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{ij}^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{ij}^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the pruning rate, which is formulated as</span></p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{ij}^{*}\}=\arg\min_{\{\alpha_{ij}\}}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}\,\alpha_{ij}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{ij}^{*}\}=\arg\min_{\{\alpha_{ij}\}}\sum_{i,j}H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}\,\alpha_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">subject to</span></p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i,j}\alpha_{ij}=r\,\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i,j}\alpha_{ij}=r\,\|\mathbf{W}\|_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As a result, the value of <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> determines whether the weight <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> should be pruned or not.
We use the term <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}\;:=\;H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}\;:=\;H_{ij,ij}\,W_{ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">and name <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> as the important score to measure the effect of the parameter <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> on the model’s performance, where a higher score means that the parameter has a more powerful effect on the loss.
Therefore, the optimal strategy is to prune the weights whose importance scores are smallest, until exactly an <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of the parameters is selected.
Equivalently, one is able to set</span></p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{ij}^{*}=\begin{cases}1,&amp;S_{ij}\leq\tau\\
0,&amp;S_{ij}&gt;\tau\end{cases}\quad\#\{(i,j)\mid s_{ij}\leq\tau\}=r\,\lvert\mathbf{W}\rvert_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">#</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{ij}^{*}=\begin{cases}1,&amp;S_{ij}\leq\tau\\
0,&amp;S_{ij}&gt;\tau\end{cases}\quad\#\{(i,j)\mid s_{ij}\leq\tau\}=r\,\lvert\mathbf{W}\rvert_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#\{\cdot\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#\{\cdot\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of elements in a set, so that <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{\mathbf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math> is fully determined by thresholding the scores <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To illustrate the pruning process, we utilize a representative algorithm named Wanda <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> as an example.
Specifically, for a standard fully connected layer, Wanda computes <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{ij,ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{ij,ij}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{ij,ij}\approx\tfrac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\bigl(x_{j}^{(m)}\bigr)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{ij,ij}\approx\tfrac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\bigl(x_{j}^{(m)}\bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where the activation vector for channel <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> over the input of the calibration set <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x^{(m)}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x^{(m)}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{j}=[x_{j}^{(1)},\dots,x_{j}^{(M)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{j}=[x_{j}^{(1)},\dots,x_{j}^{(M)}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the important score <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}=\tfrac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\bigl(x_{j}^{(m)}\bigr)^{2}\cdot W_{i,j}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}=\tfrac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\bigl(x_{j}^{(m)}\bigr)^{2}\cdot W_{i,j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{M}\bigl(x_{j}^{(m)}\bigr)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{M}\bigl(x_{j}^{(m)}\bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the square of the activation L2 norm <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{X}_{j}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\sum_{m=1}^{M}(x_{j}^{(m)})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐗</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{X}_{j}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\sum_{m=1}^{M}(x_{j}^{(m)})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting the average activation strength of channel <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{W}_{ij}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{W}_{ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the square of the weight of the connection <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, representing its magnitude.
This score <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> combines weight magnitude with activation strength, with a higher value indicating a more important role the weight plays in the LLM.
In other words, given a pruning rate <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the parameters whose score <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is ranked on the bottom-<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> are pruned.
</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Task-Specific Pruning</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For task-specific LLM utilization, the most obvious characteristic is that
<span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">feature</span> distribution differs from that of general-purpose scenarios.
The pruning thus must account for task-related features to ensure that calibration-driven pruning aligns with such distribution and task requirements.
<span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Therefore, given feature distribution from the general domain <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and the task-specific domain <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, the goal is to utilize two calibration datasets with one (denoted as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>) from the general domain (i.e., <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{G}\sim\mathcal{D}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{G}\sim\mathcal{D}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the other (denoted as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) from the target task domain (i.e., <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{T}\sim\mathcal{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{T}\sim\mathcal{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) for pruning.
Therefore, the loss function of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is written as</span></p>
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\mathbf{W})=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{G}\cup\mathcal{D}_{T}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∪</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\mathbf{W})=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{G}\cup\mathcal{D}_{T}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> may not be independent with each other,
we define three disjoint subsets of the calibration data, namely, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{G-}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{T-}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{GT}=\mathcal{D}_{G}\cap\mathcal{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∩</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{GT}=\mathcal{D}_{G}\cap\mathcal{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{G-}=\mathcal{D}_{G}\setminus\mathcal{D}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{G-}=\mathcal{D}_{G}\setminus\mathcal{D}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E14Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{T-}=\mathcal{D}_{T}\setminus\mathcal{D}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{T-}=\mathcal{D}_{T}\setminus\mathcal{D}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of samples shared by both the general domain and the task-specific domain, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{G-}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of samples unique to the general domain, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{T-}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of samples unique to the task-specific domain.
Therfore, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{G-}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{T-}</annotation></semantics></math> are mutually disjoint and we decompose Eq. (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In II-B Task-Specific Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) to</span></p>
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\mathbf{W})\;=\;L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})\;+\;L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})\;+\;L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\mathbf{W})\;=\;L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})\;+\;L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})\;+\;L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math> are the losses for the shared, general-only and the task-specific-only domains and are computed by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{GT}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{GT}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{G-}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{G-}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E16Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{T-}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}_{T-}}\bigl[\ell(f_{\mathbf{W}}(x),y^{*})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Following Eq. (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we expand the mixed loss at <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> by a second-order Taylor series and neglect the first-order term, and obtain</span></p>
<table id="S2.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta L(\mathbf{W})\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta L(\mathbf{W})\approx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H_{GT}\Delta\mathbf{W}+\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H_{G-}\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H_{GT}\Delta\mathbf{W}+\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H_{G-}\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E17Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H_{T-}\Delta\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\mathbf{W}^{\top}H_{T-}\Delta\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where</span></p>
<table id="S2.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{GT}=\nabla^{2}L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{GT}=\nabla^{2}L_{GT}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{G-}=\nabla^{2}L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{G-}=\nabla^{2}L_{G-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{T-}=\nabla^{2}L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐖</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{T-}=\nabla^{2}L_{T-}(\mathbf{W})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">are the Hessian matrices for the shared, general-only, and the task-specific-only domains, respectively.
Following the process of Eq. (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)-(<a href="#S2.E10" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), task-specific pruning computes the important score <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> by the sum of the important scores from the shared, general-only, and the task-specific-only domains (which are denoted as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}^{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}^{GT}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}^{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}^{G-}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}^{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}^{T-}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively) by</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=S_{ij}^{GT}+S_{ij}^{G-}+S_{ij}^{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=S_{ij}^{GT}+S_{ij}^{G-}+S_{ij}^{T-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To compute the pruning scores for different groups, we need to divide the data features from the general domain and the task-specific domains into the three groups, i.e., the features shared by both the general and task-specific domains, the ones unique to the general domain, and the ones unique to the task-specific domain.
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To this end, we design an approach based on the difference in activation magnitudes.
Specifically, for channel <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in a given layer (assume the total number of channels is <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>), we compute its activation norms over the general domain calibration set, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x_{j}^{(G)}|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x_{j}^{(G)}|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and over the task-specific domain calibration set, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x_{j}^{(T)}|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x_{j}^{(T)}|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then form the difference score <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{j}=|x_{j}^{(G)}|_{2}-|x_{j}^{(T)}|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{j}=|x_{j}^{(G)}|_{2}-|x_{j}^{(T)}|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We then sort all channels by <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in descending order and divide them according to a positive hyperparameter <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>: channels with <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{j}&gt;\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{j}&gt;\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are classified as general-only, those with <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\alpha&lt;\Delta_{j}&lt;\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\alpha&lt;\Delta_{j}&lt;\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are task-only, and those with <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are treated as shared.
Intuitively, this means that if a channel’s activation in the general domain exceeds that in the task-specific domain by more than <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, it is general-only; if it is lower by more than <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, it is task-only; and if the difference is within the range <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-\alpha,\alpha]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-\alpha,\alpha]</annotation></semantics></math>, it is classified as shared.
For each group, we use the following approach to compute the pruning scores for the parameters.
First, for the general-domain-only channels (index set <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{G-}</annotation></semantics></math>), we compute the pruning score using the examples from the general domain.
Similarly, for the task-specific domain channels (index set <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{T-}</annotation></semantics></math>), we compute the pruning score using the examples from the task-specific domain.
For shared channels (index set <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math>), we compute the pruning score using the sum of pruning scores from both the general and the task-specific domain.
Therefore, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}^{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}^{GT}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}^{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}^{G-}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}^{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}^{T-}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{ij}^{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{ij}^{GT}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{ij}^{G}+s_{ij}^{T},\quad j\in\mathcal{J}_{GT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{ij}^{G}+s_{ij}^{T},\quad j\in\mathcal{J}_{GT}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E21Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{ij}^{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{ij}^{G-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{ij}^{G},\quad j\in\mathcal{J}_{G-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{ij}^{G},\quad j\in\mathcal{J}_{G-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E21Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S_{ij}^{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S_{ij}^{T-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E21Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{ij}^{T},\quad j\in\mathcal{J}_{T-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{ij}^{T},\quad j\in\mathcal{J}_{T-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{ij}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{ij}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are the pruning scores obtained through the standard pruning process using the general domain and the task-specific domain data, respectively.
Because <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i,j}^{GT}=S_{i,j}^{G}+S_{i,j}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i,j}^{GT}=S_{i,j}^{G}+S_{i,j}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for shared channels, this naturally makes the shared score twice that of any exclusive score, reflecting its higher importance and matching the intuition that the parameters for the shared part of the domains should be more important than the parameters for only one domain.
Finally, we sort all mixed importance scores <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> in the entire model from smallest to largest and prune away the lowest <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of parameters according to the target sparsity rate <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using the Wanda pruning algorithm as an example.
For each parameter <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, Wanda computes a pruning score <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> following Eq. (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In II-A LLM Pruning ‣ II The Approach ‣ Frustratingly Easy Task-aware Pruning forLarge Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).
This score corresponds to the effect of pruning the weight <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> on the loss under the task-specific settings, balancing the parameter sensitivities of the general and task-specific domains.
We sort all parameters based on their mixed pruning score <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We iteratively prune the weights with the lowest scores until the predetermined pruning ratio <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is met.
</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S2.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE I</span>: </span><span id="S2.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Overall results on WikiText-2 (WT-2) (PPL), MMLU, MedQA, and ARC for Qwen-3 (32B) at various compression ratios (CR), where the performance of the original LLM without pruning is also reported for reference.
Lower perplexity on WT-2 and higher accuracy on other datasets indicate better performance, which are marked by <math id="S2.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
“Avg.” refers to the average performance on MMLU, MedQA, and ARC.
</span>
</span></figcaption>
